# WHAT PRETTIER MUST NOT TOUCH, AND THE ONE REASON ANYTHING IS HERE.
#
# `packages/term/src/doc/` holds two components copied CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER out of the
# repository's own `README.md`, so that a rendering backend written from outside can be shown
# running the project's published documentation rather than a component written to suit it.
# `packages/term/src/readme-verbatim.test.ts` compares the two files byte for byte and fails if
# they diverge.
#
# The README's code is not prettier-clean under this repository's own config — `exoDerive(count,
# c => …)` would gain parentheses under `arrowParens: "always"` — so formatting the copy would
# make it stop matching the original, and the test would fail on a `npm run format`. Formatting
# the README instead would change what every reader of this project sees first, for the
# convenience of one private package.
#
# Nothing else belongs in this file. If a second entry ever appears, the question to ask is
# whether it has the same shape of reason: a file whose exact bytes are asserted somewhere else.
packages/term/src/doc/
